[{"category":"section","location":"index.html#TWA.jl","page":"Home","text":"TWA.jl provides a unified interface for truncated-Wigner approximations for interacting spin systems.\n\nThe package separates four concepts:\n\nmodel = SpinModel(\n    Chain(50),\n    XXZ(J=1.0, Δ=0.5),\n)\n\nstate = DomainWall()\n\nmethod = DTWA(\n    trajectories=1000,\n)\n\nresult = simulate(\n    model,\n    state,\n    method;\n    tspan=(0, 12),\n) \n\nThe same model and state can be simulated using different approximations, including DTWA and CTWA.  ","title":"TWA.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#DTWA-and-CTWA","page":"Home","text":"The same model and initial state can be evolved using different truncated-Wigner approximations.\n\n(Image: DTWA and CTWA magnetization comparison)","title":"DTWA and CTWA"}]
